---
# Register-level code lives by different rules than the algorithm libs:
# - MMIO access is by definition a fixed-address dereference (the CMSIS
#   peripheral pointers are casts of fixed addresses).
# - Datasheet values (sensor register encodings, field values, pin and
#   timing numbers) are the domain language; naming each one would obscure
#   the reference document they mirror.
# - Service lifecycle methods (init, poll, send) touch peripheral registers
#   instead of members; making them static or const would betray the
#   injectable service pattern for a property of the register map.
# - The vector table and FPU enable are built from linker symbols at file
#   scope, which is the whole point of a startup file.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
    -clang-analyzer-core.FixedAddressDereference,
    -cppcoreguidelines-interfaces-global-init,
    -readability-convert-member-functions-to-static,
    -readability-magic-numbers,
    -readability-make-member-function-const
...
